 "substitutedBy": null,
 "summary": "Legalizes, validates, ratifies and confirms the actions of the Panama central school district regardless of the failure of such district to timely file final building cost reports.",
 "title": "Legalizes, validates, ratifies and confirms the actions of the Panama central school district regardless of the failure of such district to timely file final building cost reports",
 "vetoMessages": {
  "items": [
   {
    "billId": {
     "basePrintNo": "A8926",
     "basePrintNoStr": "A8926-2019",
     "printNo": "A8926",
     "session": 2019,
     "version": ""
    },
    "billPage": 0,
    "chapter": 0,
    "lineEnd": 0,
    "lineStart": 0,
    "memoText": "\n \n                          VETO MESSAGE - No. 56\n \nTO THE ASSEMBLY:\n \nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bills:\n \nAssembly Bill Number 8926, entitled:\n \n    \"AN ACT to legalize, validate, ratify and confirm the actions of the\n      Panama  central  school  district  notwithstanding  the failure to\n      timely file final building cost reports with the education depart-\n      ment\"\n \nAssembly Bill Number 9922, entitled:\n \n    \"AN ACT in relation to  authorizing  the  Liverpool  central  school\n      district  to receive state aid for certain approved capital funded\n      projects\"\n \nAssembly Bill Number 9951, entitled:\n \n    \"AN ACT relating to legalizing, validating, ratifying and confirming\n      a transportation contract of the Fulton city school district\"\n \n    NOT APPROVED\n\n  Each of these bills would authorize, outside of the State budget proc-\ness, payment of State expense-based  education  aid  above  the  amounts\ncalculated and previously agreed to under current law.\n \n  These  bills  would  forgive the return of State building aid payments\nfrom the Panama Central School District and the Liverpool Central School\nDistrict and would reverse  disallowance  of  State  transportation  aid\npayments to the Fulton City School District.\n \n  Identical  legislation  for  each  of  these school districts has been\nvetoed in prior years. The payments withheld  or  to  be  recovered  for\nthese school districts each are a result of violation of State laws that\nwere  known  to the districts at the time, and related to the districts'\nfailure to properly obtain authorization for  expenses  reimbursable  by\nthe State.\n \n  In  both the 2017 and 2018 State Budgets, the Legislature and I agreed\nto payment provisions  to  mitigate  outstanding  filing  penalties  for\nschool  districts. As well, some of these school districts have benefit-\nted from special legislation adopted in the budget to extend the payback\nperiod for their respective penalties, and have received legislative aid\nthrough the budget.\n \n  In addition to these previously-vetoed bills, I  have  vetoed  several\nsimilar  bills in the past due to their financial impacts outside of the\nState budget process. While bills of this nature have infrequently  been\nsigned  due  to  extenuating  circumstances,  these present bills do not\ncontain such circumstances; and in fact  due  to  the  unique  financial\nsituation  we  are  in  now,  it  weighs heavily against making any such\ndetermination this year.\n \n  These bills would create new financial obligations not  accounted  for\nwithin  the  State's  financial  plan.  Such funding decisions should be\naddressed within the context of the annual  budget  negotiations.  These\nbills  would also violate existing agreements that were previously nego-\ntiated  with the Legislature during the budget negotiation process. I am\ntherefore constrained to veto these bills.\n \n  These bills are disapproved.                (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n \n                               __________\n",
    "signedDate": null,
    "signer": "ANDREW M. CUOMO",
    "vetoNumber": 56,
